{
  "schema": 2,
  "id": "domains",
  "name": "Domains",
  "version": "1.1.1",
  "description": "Reverse proxy with free, automatically renewed HTTPS certificates. Point your own domains at this NAS and forward them to any host and port - another device, a container, or EthOS itself - without touching nginx by hand. Caddy issues and renews Let's Encrypt certificates on its own, and the stack keeps routing even when EthOS is restarting.",
  "icon": "🌐",
  "icon_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SyncHot/ethos-packages/main/domains/icon.svg",
  "category": "network",
  "author": "SyncHot",
  "homepage": "https://github.com/SyncHot/ethos-packages",
  "license": "MIT",
  "channel": "stable",
  "ui": {
    "mode": "native",
    "entry": "frontend/app.js",
    "port": 8093
  },
  "healthcheck": {
    "scheme": "http",
    "port": 8093,
    "path": "/api/health"
  },
  "changelog": "1.1.1: read certificates from Caddy's actual storage root (/data/caddy/certificates), so the certificate list and expiry show up. per-route response headers and permanent redirects, plus a bulk route import so an existing proxy configuration (for example Nginx Proxy Manager) can be migrated in one step. 1.0.0: initial release: Caddy-based reverse proxy with automatic Let's Encrypt certificates, per-domain routes to any host:port (including EthOS itself), WebSocket and streaming support, live certificate expiry, a DNS preflight check and the proxy log in one native EthOS window.",
